1
00:00:00,250 --> 00:00:02,936
Forty trucks on channel nineteen.

2
00:00:02,936 --> 00:00:04,890
Only my radio heard him.

3
00:00:05,490 --> 00:00:07,604
December, two thousand one.

4
00:00:07,604 --> 00:00:08,386
Ice storm.

5
00:00:08,386 --> 00:00:09,560
Missouri hills.

6
00:00:09,560 --> 00:00:15,040
A calm voice told me to stop at a
white post, right before the bridge.

7
00:00:15,640 --> 00:00:17,793
I said, not on a hill.

8
00:00:17,793 --> 00:00:18,870
Not on ice.

9
00:00:19,470 --> 00:00:21,480
He said, "Don't argue with me, son."

10
00:00:22,080 --> 00:00:23,060
So I stopped.

11
00:00:23,660 --> 00:00:27,440
Four minutes later, three trucks
folded across that bridge.

12
00:00:28,040 --> 00:00:30,598
Next morning, I told my dispatcher.

13
00:00:30,598 --> 00:00:33,009
She went quiet for a full minute.

14
00:00:33,009 --> 00:00:34,690
Then she said his name.

15
00:00:35,290 --> 00:00:37,180
And I still don't know why, out of
